<!-- ================================================================ DISCOVERY -->
<section class="panel" id="tab-discovery" data-name="discovery">
{{ plain('discovery') }}
<h2>Target discovery: promising, little studied, no drug yet</h2>
<p class="lede">The screen starts from <strong>{{ D.pool }}</strong> genes that rise in UC in the meta-analysis of eight cohorts (padj &lt; 0.05, log2FC ≥ 1, at least two cohorts). Each gene is then checked for how much of its rise survives the composition adjustment (a tissue change, not cells arriving), which cell family makes it, how much UC literature it has (Europe PMC), whether a clinical drug exists (Open Targets), whether it looks tractable, and how much it is expressed in vital organs (Human Protein Atlas). A gene is a <strong>first-in-class opportunity</strong> when it keeps at least half of its rise after adjustment, has few UC papers and no clinical drug, is tractable and stays at or below 50 nTPM in every vital organ ({{ kpis.fic }} genes: {% for t, n in D.fic_by_track.items() %}{{ n }} {{ t }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}). These are hypotheses ranked by data, not validated targets.</p>
{{ paras(f.narrative.sections.discovery or []) }}
<div class="kpis">
  {% for t, n in D.by_track.items() %}<div class="kpi"><b>{{ n }}</b><span>{{ t }} track</span></div>{% endfor %}
  {% for k, v in D.status.items() %}<div class="kpi"><b>{{ v }}</b><span>{{ k }}</span></div>{% endfor %}
</div>
<div class="grid two">
  {{ plot('discovery_scatter', figs.discovery_scatter) }}{{ plot('discovery_bars', figs.discovery_bars) }}
</div>
<h3>Spotlight: first-in-class candidates</h3>
<p class="small">The best first-in-class genes of each cell family after the checks of the Validation shortlist (its groups A, then B, in its order), so a gene the checks place in group C is not shown here even if its novelty score is high. Novelty score ({% for k, v in D.weights.items() %}{{ k | replace("_"," ") }} {{ v }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}; it only orders the list, the filters decide the status).</p>
<div class="grid">
{% for r in D.cards %}
<div class="card cand claim" data-evidence="{{ r.evidence_ids | evattr }}">
  <h3>{{ r.gene }} <span class="small">{{ r.name or "" }}</span></h3>
  <div class="meta"><span class="tag {{ r.track }}">{{ r.track }} #{{ r.rank_in_track }}</span><span class="tag fic">first-in-class</span>{% if r.group %}<span class="tag">shortlist group {{ r.group }}</span>{% endif %}
    <span class="tag">novelty {{ r.novelty }}</span><span class="tag">{{ r.papers }} UC papers</span>
    <span class="tag">kept {{ "%.0f" | format(100 * r.retained) }} %</span>{% if r.pocket %}<span class="tag">pocket {{ r.pocket }}</span>{% endif %}</div>
