<h2>Limitations</h2>
<ul>{% for l in f.narrative.limitations %}<li>{{ l.text }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
<h2>What is still missing</h2>
<ul class="roadmap">
<li>Nothing here was tested in the laboratory or in patients; the first-in-class genes have never been studied in a mouse colitis model and need knock-down or antibody experiments in organoids or colitis models.</li>
<li>Protein in the gut wall is measured in one proteomics study, but no genetic resource exists for mucosal protein levels (pQTL), so causal genetics uses blood protein and gut RNA.</li>
<li>The Visium deconvolution relies on one single-cell atlas; co-occurring cell groups (inflammatory fibroblasts and neutrophils in ulcers) are hard to separate. CosMx does not resolve those candidates and no Visium HD data of UC are public.</li>
<li>CXCR2, OSM, DUOX2 and TNF have no genetic instrument in any layer.</li>
<li>Treatment-response arms other than UNIFI and PROTECT are small; no gene separates a drug from placebo after correction, and the anti-TNF single-cell cohort has six remitters.</li>
<li>No blood proteomics of patients: the report cannot say which tissue biomarkers can be measured in blood.</li>
<li>"Undrugged" uses Open Targets, not company pipelines, trial registries or patents.</li>
</ul>
